    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "RAY COOKE AUCTIONEERS proudly present this two bedroom, extended, semi-detached bungalow to the market tucked away within this highly sought after development. Cherrywood Avenue continues to be in high demand and will be equally sought after between first time buyers looking to step onto the property ladder and clients downsizing seeking mature and established surroundings. Within walking distance you will find Corkagh Park, Clondalkin Village and a host of shops, schools and leisure facilities, not to mention the M50 Motorway and The Luas all within a couple of minutes' drive. Interior living accommodation of c. 71 Sqm comprises of entrance hallway, living room, extended kitchen/breakfast room, two bedrooms and family bathroom. Externally this property benefits from a private, EAST facing rear garden with side access to the front which offers a driveway for off road parking. No. 35 was originally constructed as a 3 bedroom bungalow but has been remodelled over the years into its current form as a two bed. This property is in good condition throughout but offer a prime opportunity for its next occupants to purchase a well located property and put their own stamp on it. Due to location, price and type of property we know this will be extremely popular so early viewing is highly advised, Call Ray Cooke Auctioneers today.\n\nKey Features\nBER D\nSqm 71\nPrivate EAST facing garden\nGood condition throughout\nTwo bedrooms\nNo onward chain\nEasy access to N7 & M50\nHighly popular development\nClose to Clondalkin Village\nDriveway to front\nClose to all local amenities\nDouble glazed windows\n\nDirections\nFrom the junction at Newlands Cross, head towards Clondalkin along the Fonthill road and continue past the Cross roads, after roughly 1km you will reach a round about and you want to take the 3rd exit onto. Once on Cherrywood Road, take the 3rd left turn and No. 35 will be just on your right hand side."
      },
      {
